# Design system

- **Direction:** content-first dark UI in the family of the Apple TV app and YouTube TV. Video and artwork fill the screen; navigation and controls float above them on Liquid Glass (Apple) or `backdrop-filter` glass (web). Dark is the default; light mode follows the system on iPhone and web.
- **Tokens:** `design/tokens.json` is the single source for color, category tints, type scale, spacing, radii, elevation, and motion. It generates `web/src/theme/tokens.css` and `apple/Packages/BroadwaveUI/Sources/BroadwaveUI/Theme+Tokens.swift` (`node design/build.mjs`). Change tokens there, never in outputs.
- **Type:** SF Pro on Apple (system font), `system-ui` then Inter on web. Tabular numbers for times, channel numbers, and scores.
- **Color:** a neutral near-black canvas; one user-selectable accent (default electric blue); red is reserved for live and recording. Category tints (Sports, News, Movies, Kids, Series) are subtle backgrounds in the guide, never text colors.
- **Information density:** show what helps a decision. The live badge shows progress; a recording dot marks what will record; "behind live" appears only when behind. Technical details (codec, bitrate, signal, sync offset) live in the Stream Info panel.
- **Motion:** springs for navigation and focus, quick fades for chrome. Everything respects Reduce Motion and Reduce Transparency.
- **10-foot:** focus is scale plus glass plus shadow, never just an outline. Minimum TV body text is 29 pt equivalent.
